## Context

Reading-2 finding 41 (tracker 0578), author's words: "Condense to 1.5
pages. State: we will continue towards a method that scores all green
on Table S1 — finds all the projects, only the projects, each
justified by 2 primary sources, with correct attributes. That method
requires research on 6 axes: information fusion, external coherence
scoring, tracking both events and states, knowledge base architecture,
replication on country and sectors. Reorder the axes; weave the
literature review with the 6 axes instead of juxtaposing. (Author
invites pushback on ordering.)"

Note: the author says 6 axes but the enumeration parses to 5–6
(replication on countries / on sectors may be one axis or two).
Reconcile against the current §9 content and state the resolution in
the PR description.

## Relevant files

- `slides/manuscript/main.tex` — sec:future (L1103–1224); the current
  axis list and the juxtaposed related-work passages
- `docs/editorial-brief.md` — `kb-programme-items` (three KB design
  items at no-spoiler altitude) and `no-companion-paper-promise`: both
  constrain this rewrite
- `.claude/rules/writing.md` — Related Work citation-budget and
  per-paragraph-mix rules apply to the woven literature

## Actions

1. Condense §9 to ≤1.5 rendered pages.
2. Open with the goal statement (all-green on Table S1: find all the
   projects, only the projects, each justified by 2 primary sources,
   with correct attributes).
3. Restructure around the research axes; PROPOSE a reasoned ordering
   (the author invites pushback — put the rationale in the PR
   description, e.g. dependency order vs impact order; do not block
   waiting for input).
4. Weave the literature into each axis instead of juxtaposing a
   review block; respect the citation-budget rules.

